        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georg Cantor, Vladimir Arnold\n- Concepts: transfinite number, transfinite\n- Topics: mathematics\n\nFacts:\n- Georg Cantor was born on March 3, 1845, and he was a German mathematician.\n- Georg Cantor coined the term \"transfinite\" to avoid some implications of the word \"infinite\" for objects that were not finite.\n- Vladimir Arnold was born on June 12, 1937, and he was a Soviet and Russian mathematician.\n- Georg Cantor died on January 6, 1918.\n- Vladimir Arnold died on June 3, 2010.",
